--- Rosetta Code: Keyboard input/Obtain a Y or N response
--- https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Keyboard_input/Obtain_a_Y_or_N_response
--- Partial: Crow reads standard input a line at a time and has no terminal
--- control, so it can neither flush the keys pressed before the question nor
--- take a key without Enter. The answer is therefore a line: lines are read
--- until one holds Y or N (either case, spaces around it ignored), and any
--- other line asks again. The end of the input is no answer.

--- the first line answering the question with Y or N, as 'Y' or 'N'
fn ask[question]
    line = input['`question` (Y/N) ']
    while line.ok
        key = upper[trim[line]]
        if key eq 'Y' or key eq 'N'
            return key
        log['\'`line`\' is neither Y nor N.']
        line = input['`question` (Y/N) ']
    return error['the input ended before a Y or an N', 'input']

for question in ['Continue?', 'Save the changes?', 'Quit?']
    answer = ask[question]
    if answer.ok
        log['You answered `answer`.']
    else
        log['No answer: `answer.reason`.']
